#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
RAM26 Alpha Engine v1
====================

Purpose
-------
Generate RAM26 target weights from fresh alpha features and publish them through a
strict, fail-closed contract that is compatible with the v4 Sleeve-Primary/Bridge
repair path.

Design invariants
-----------------
1. No 1/N fallback. If the signal is flat, stale, missing, or unsafe, the engine
   refuses to publish tradeable targets.
2. Preserve alpha dispersion. Output targets must pass CV/unique-weight guards.
3. Safe by default. The engine writes RAM26 staging keys by default and never
   writes ssot:target:v2:current unless explicitly unlocked.
4. No broker orders. This file only emits target JSON; order execution must remain
   downstream and separately gated.

Typical commands
----------------
# One-shot Redis read -> RAM26 output key
python3 Ram26_alpha_engine_v1.py --once --publish-redis

# PM2/service loop
python3 Ram26_alpha_engine_v1.py --loop --publish-redis --cycle-sec 5

# Local file dry-run
python3 Ram26_alpha_engine_v1.py --once --input-json features.json --output-json out.json --no-strict-freshness

# Deterministic self-test
python3 Ram26_alpha_engine_v1.py --self-test

Expected Redis input formats
----------------------------
The engine accepts either of these forms at RAM26_FEATURES_KEY:

1) Redis HASH
   key:   ram26:features:v1
   field: <symbol>
   value: JSON object containing features

2) Redis STRING
   key:   ram26:features:v1
   value: JSON list/dict with feature records

Supported feature aliases include ret_5d/mom_5d, ret_20d/mom_20d,
ret_60d/mom_60d, vol_20d/volatility_20d, quality/quality_score,
value/value_score, liquidity/liquidity_score, sentiment/sentiment_score,
drawdown_20d/max_drawdown_20d, spread_bps, updated_at_ms.
"""

